------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Redwood / Visual Builder renderer (frontend/web/monorepo/apps/redwood)
integrates with Oracle JET (Universal Permissive License 1.0) and loads Oracle
Spectra / Visual Builder Runtime from Oracle's CDN. Those components are NOT
part of this project and are NOT relicensed here; see
frontend/web/monorepo/apps/redwood/NOTICE.md for details.

All other renderers and the Mateu runtime, annotations, wire DTOs, generated
schemas and tooling are licensed under Apache License 2.0.

The web renderer bundles (the io.mateu:vaadin-lit jar) include third-party
open-source packages under permissive licences (MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, ISC and
similar); scripts/check-frontend-licenses.mjs lists the approved licences and
fails the build on any other, so no commercially licensed component is shipped.
One of them carries a condition:

  bpmn-js (Camunda Services GmbH, bpmn.io License): MIT terms plus the
  requirement that the bpmn.io watermark shown on rendered diagrams stays fully
  visible and is not removed, changed or overlapped. Mateu's BPMN component
  keeps it as bpmn-js renders it.

The Map component draws OpenStreetMap tiles by default (map data
© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL). The public OSM tile servers are not meant
for heavy production traffic: deployments should configure their own provider.
